Gale king is in Philadelphia this  morning where she had an interview with  Starbucks executive chairman Howard  Schultz about the company's plan to  train its workers to avoid bias Gayle  joins us now from inside that Starbucks  store and Gail I know you asked him to  about whether he saw that video of those  two men being arrested Norah you're  right you know me very well video  showing that arrest has now been seen  worldwide  so we asked Howard Schultz about his  reaction to that now infamous footage  and the issue of unconscious racial bias  I first saw it on Friday I couldn't  believe it I was I was sick to my  stomach I was embarrassed I was ashamed  this is the antithesis of the values and  culture of everything Starbucks stands  for it stands where you founded this  company to foster human experience yes  so this was an Anatomy tonight however  it's undeniable when you look at the  tape that we are responsible that I  personally am responsible and we need to  address it with transparency and honesty  and we we all got on a plane and came to  Philadelphia we all who is that Kevin  Johnson myself you've said your team  yeah the senior team and I think this  was a galvanizing moment for the entire  company we have issues in our company  that we need to recognize and in  recognizing that we decided we're going  to close every single store at great  expense yeah for retraining but it won't  won't stop there we have been on a  journey to talk about race in America  it's a very difficult subject raised to  talking about race makes people very  uncomfortable  but you say let's go there I think in  other country has systemic issues  certainly there's a great divide in the  country it's a great device race in  America I'm not saying that Starbucks in  any way has an anecdote to fix it but  perhaps we can use this moment as a  healing moment for our company and in  doing so given the fact that we serve so  many millions of people and employ  hundreds of thousands of people we can  use this as an opportunity to educate  you just said when you looked at the  tape you were heartsick but did you  think it was an isolated incident and  I'm asking that because now I'm hearing  more and more stories from people I know  strangers on the street are saying you  know what I had an incident at Starbucks  I'm not surprised to hear this I think  it's possible that given the level of  unconscious bias that exists in America  and how systemic this problem is in the  country that this is not an isolated  situation and if it's not we will deal  with every one of them I want to  personally apologize for anyone who has  ever felt anything other than respect  and dignity in our stores and I've said  publicly for years at regardless of the  color skin your sexual orientation your  politics  you are welcome at Starbucks what does  Starbucks plan to do to make people more  accountable for these  we're reviewing every single policy and  we're communicating directly with our  people so that they understand that  calling 9-1-1 because to  african-american young men are sitting  in our stores it's absolutely the wrong  thing to do what is the definition of  trespassing in Starbucks I mean people  come in here all the time they're some  of them are eating Starbucks things some  of them aren't what is a definition of  trespassing this is a place where  everybody comes nobody should be asked  to leave Starbucks now this is the third  place between home and work we serve  millions of people so I don't want to  ask anyone to leave now there are  certain situations where people are not  acting appropriately either they're  homeless or they're they have mental  health issues that was not the case here  this was absolutely not the case here so  we want to be an inviting welcoming  place for everyone Howard Schultz told  me there is no textbook on how to handle  something like this he said really all  you can do is operate on instinct and  heart he said it was deeply personal and  I felt that I felt really that his pain  was palpable when I was talking to him  today he's arranging now a meeting  between the manager and the two young  black men and I said do the young black  men want to meet with her yes and she  wants to meet with him with them she's  been getting death threats they're  concerned about her safety but Howard  says this is not a one-off he intends to  see this through so back to you guys in  the studio I also have to tell you this  I tried very hard to get Howard to come  to the table yesterday because I thought  it would be great to have him in the  studio and I think I might have pushed  too hard because finally just said Gail  I cannot do it I have all these meetings  in Philadelphia I'm happy to talk to you  all but I cannot come to New York so I  was delighted he agreed to meet with us  in a Starbucks because that was an issue  too few people can say no to you Gail  but you know aside from that being the  right moral decision on his part is the  right business decision - in Wall Street  it's rewarding him for that Gail thank  you
 

